    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/web-emilea-may.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/island-proud-with-emilea-may/?occurrence=2024-08-28"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/island-proud-with-emilea-may/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Welcome to Island Proud, where we'll present the best in PEI talent and hospitality! Island Proud features a 45 minute concert followed by a reception in the pavilion with the artist.  Emilea May is a Prince Edward Island based songstress known for crafting music that serves as a catalyst for healing and growth through raw expression. With her dreamy vocals and honest lyrics that cut to the core, her music provokes deep-feeling and introspection. Drawing inspiration from artists like Lizzy McAlpine and Madison Cunningham, she weaves tales inspired by the mysteries of creation, the intricacies of human connection and the transformative journey of motherhood. Her forthcoming debut album “Unwreck Me” has an indie/pop/rock feel and delves deep into heartache, heaviness, and holding onto hope. In her short time performing live, she has shared the stage with artists such as Basia Bulat, Catherine MacLellan &amp; The East Pointers  Click here for more information!      Emilea May est une chanteuse basée à l'Île-du-Prince-Édouard connue pour créer une musique qui sert de catalyseur de guérison et de croissance grâce à l'expression brute. Avec sa voix rêveuse et ses paroles honnêtes qui vont à l’essentiel, sa musique provoque un sentiment profond et une introspection. S'inspirant d'artistes comme Lizzy McAlpine et Madison Cunningham, elle tisse des contes inspirés par les mystères de la création, les subtilités de la connexion humaine et le voyage transformateur de la maternité. Son prochain album, « Unwreck Me », a un côté indie/pop/rock et plonge profondément dans le chagrin, la lourdeur et l’espoir. Au cours de sa courte période de concert, elle a partagé la scène avec des artistes tels que Basia Bulat, Catherine MacLellan et The East Pointers.  &nbsp;    Cliquez ici pour plus d'information!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Island Proud with Emilea May"
      }
    ],
