        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/rose-cousins-trio/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A native of Prince Edward Island, Rose Cousins lives in Halifax Nova Scotia. Her songwriting plumbs the depths of the human condition. Her work has garnered her two JUNO Awards (2013’s We Have Made a Spark &amp; 2021’s Bravado), two Canadian Folk Music Awards, eleven East Coast Music Awards and one Grammy nomination (2018’s Natural Conclusion), along with praise from the likes of the CBC, No Depression, LA Times, Associated Press, Billboard, Folk Alley, and NPR, who raved “Cousins’ disarmingly fluid vocal tone has the ability to convey the most internalized feelings without an ounce of fuss.” Over the years, she has shared stages with Patty Griffin, Mary Chapin Carpenter, Jann Arden, Kathleen Edwards, Joe Henry and Anais Mitchell, and her music has fittingly underscored scenes from notable TV shows including Grey’s Anatomy, Fire Country, Batwoman and Heartland.  Her most recent album, 2025's Conditions of Love, Vol. 1 released in March and was followed by a headline tour across Canada."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Rose Cousins Trio"
      }
    ],
