    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/OAOrch-JL25.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/okavango-african-orchestra/?occurrence=2025-07-25"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/okavango-african-orchestra/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This is a special event! Prior to the concert, Under the Spire will be hosting an African Market in our pavilion. Be sure to come early to experience food, handmade goods and the cultures of PEI's African community.  Vendor Applications: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScjVyqLQpJ9SAfcRnhd9y-yoNeAPh-i4Qr1xRkgFw-VodQcOA/viewform?usp=header  Sign-Up for Transportation from Charlottetown: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSffsQS4n6rzjFI3CDszA-vMmFuZ1-XfPF1ZxTNeT_rT9ripmg/viewform?usp=header  - - - - - - - - - - - - -  The JUNO award-winning group Okavango African Orchestra is an ambitious musical ensemble created by Batuki Music Society, Artistic Director Nadine McNulty assembled a cast of accomplished African-born musicians who now live in Toronto and Montreal: Daniel Nebiat (krar, composer, vocals), Kofi Ackah (percussion, composer, vocals), Tichaona Maredza (mbira, guitar, composer, vocals), Sadio Sissokho (kora, tama, djembe, composer, vocals), Ebenezer Agyekum (bass guitar, composer, vocals), Assane Seck (lead guitar, composer, vocals), Aron Nitunga (guitar, composer, vocals) and Mabinty Sylla (dance).  Unifying the melodic echoes of various African cultures, their sound transcends boundaries by seamlessly blending traditional music and instruments into a unique and harmonious fusion. Their mission is to weave a rich tapestry of sound that not only pays homage to the diverse musical heritage of the African continent but also ventures into uncharted territories, creating a musical experience that is both evocative and innovative.    Join the Okavango African Orchestra on this transformative journey as they honor the roots of African music, reinventing its expression through the marriage of tradition and innovation. Experience the magic as we intricately weave together the threads of ancient melodies, creating a tapestry that reflects the beauty, complexity, and unity found in the diverse musical cultures of Africa. This is more than just music; it’s a celebration of the vibrant tapestry that is African heritage, expressed through the universal language of harmony."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Okavango African Orchestra"
      }
    ],
