    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/LMaxwell-S5.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/lawrence-maxwell-trio/?occurrence=2025-09-05"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://underthespire.ca/events-2/lawrence-maxwell-trio/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We're going full county for Lawrence Maxwell! This concert will have a special pre-show community event sponsored by the Provincial Credit Union. Join us at 5:30 for a country-style pancake dinner &amp; Western theme photo booth!  If you're familiar with live music on PEI, you've likely heard the name Lawrence Maxwell. Maxwell cut his teeth on beer caps, rough waters, and country music. His latest album, Ballad of Miles was nominated for seven Music PEI Awards in 2023, and in 2024, he received the award for Music PEI’s ‘Entertainer of the Year.’ His music video for \"Back to Cape Breton\" was a finalist in the Canadian Independent Music Video Awards and his song \"Better You\" was selected in the Top 100 for CBC/Toyota Searchlight in 2022. As an ECMA award nominee and two-time Music P.E.I. award winner, this Prince Edward Island singer-songwriter will tell it to you like it’s folk, and sing it to you like it’s country.  His debit album Not Your Outlaw (2018) put him on the Country Music map and earned him his first Music P.E.I. Award. Maxwell followed it up in 2020 with Almost Natural, which further displayed his skill at blending the traditional sounds of folk and bluegrass with modern themes and production values. It garnered Maxwell his first East Coast Music Award nomination and an AmericanaFest-UK showcase in 2021, while proving his music’s ability to unite fans of both the old and new. Now with his latest album, Ballad Of Miles, Maxwell is poised to expand his audience even further.    If Merle Haggard’s blue-collar poetry could be combined with George Jones’ voice and Sturgill Simpson’s boundary-shattering brashness, the result might just be Lawrence Maxwell’s Ballad Of Miles. As an album steeped in love, heartbreak and laughter, it is the perfect soundtrack for these times, when every day brings a new set of challenges and unexpected gifts."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Lawrence Maxwell Trio"
      }
    ],
